{"event_type":"review","id":"ab2b22a8bea1ccac10cc8bfd9e6e057cc53d50f1dff2834b5043eee02de674f2","occurred_at":"2026-11-13T09:49:52Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/935f6d527c76683ebdb08afe267dce53ac7ad24ca2bb5b2bed5a21561313ee41","sha256":"935f6d527c76683ebdb08afe267dce53ac7ad24ca2bb5b2bed5a21561313ee41"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/c071604af6f10628d154f0ada91556ac577a7272c084b54053f7306c3ecdb10f","sha256":"c071604af6f10628d154f0ada91556ac577a7272c084b54053f7306c3ecdb10f"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/655ceaee199b7d7cd73471c19928d28e6d779d3eb188de8182c3d8f0a2483159","sha256":"655ceaee199b7d7cd73471c19928d28e6d779d3eb188de8182c3d8f0a2483159"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/7f892b73b999616e976edcd40806c284cca3f51df072ab290fdb4b1ad380d3ac","sha256":"7f892b73b999616e976edcd40806c284cca3f51df072ab290fdb4b1ad380d3ac"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/5ed1ad8c5e41fd36a62b1602b5d37e37a09399974cc7d2f9d327efbce8bcc6bc","sha256":"5ed1ad8c5e41fd36a62b1602b5d37e37a09399974cc7d2f9d327efbce8bcc6bc"}],"attempt_id":"b59d2eadfa473b51e69a70ad27a6090f2240f5ed27b9ecb9da5847782c22225e:0:1","base":"214777d9d28d7d0477f8e6b0048a692c0edc2008","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"9e55ea8c9823c34b72d58173fc1273593d246733","body":"**Keep result stdout machine-readable.**\n\nA successful recovery emits `repair recovery: {...}`, which is not JSON. The triage result at `apps/crq-python/crq_repair.py:688` has the same prefix problem. Other routes print narration to stdout without a JSON result.\n\nUse one CLI result writer to emit exactly one JSON artifact. Send status narration and worker messages to stderr.\n\nAs per coding guidelines, I1 requires “Every operation invocation writes machine-readable JSON to stdout and human narration to stderr, never mixed.”","id":"ad3a244b0a0f8f4740093ace44d37a0931eb94686803e4f56e4d54576bd3a5a0","intervals":[[1038,1038]],"path":"apps/crq-python/crq_repair.py","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Keep result stdout machine-readable."},{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"9e55ea8c9823c34b72d58173fc1273593d246733","body":"**Defer mechanical verification when the detector is unavailable.**\n\nIf `hack_detector` raises `DetectorUnavailable` after a fixer commits, `mechanical` propagates that exception into this handler (`apps/crq-python/crq_repair.py:435`). The handler records a mechanical failure and advances the fixer rung. A persistent detector outage therefore runs A1 and A2, then records `FAILED`, without obtaining a detector verdict.\n\nPreserve the candidate and resume mechanical verification without another fixer invocation. The harvest path already distinguishes this condition from a rejected patch (`apps/crq-python/repair_tick.py:456-459`).","id":"2caf9176e0a4d38e14e85be21fa94589dc11dd2c21122aa31828326cd3c7b995","intervals":[[519,519]],"path":"apps/crq-python/crq_repair.py","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Defer mechanical verification when the detector is unavailable."},{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"9e55ea8c9823c34b72d58173fc1273593d246733","body":"**Exit with code 2 for invalid selector combinations.**\n\nIf the caller supplies only `--job`, this branch prints a refusal and returns normally. The entry point at `apps/crq-python/crq_repair.py:1048` then exits 0. The conflicting recovery-selector branch has the same failure at Line 994. Automation receives a clean exit although the requested operation did not run.\n\nPropagate usage-error exit code 2 through the entry point.\n\nAs per coding guidelines, I1 requires “Exit codes: 0 clean, 1 thrown error, 2 arg error, 3 needs-human.”","id":"6089fc32cf8811c29c5cc0f9b1b2e0a3ac08b5f2c3403be4e978c61e5fb8b338","intervals":[[997,997]],"path":"apps/crq-python/crq_repair.py","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Exit with code 2 for invalid selector combinations."}],"head":"06c124be492b1d197d772fe5a48784c1e4dad0b0","head_tree":"40cca612920bd0f60b7d7ded61025db433bf3a2a","input_scope":[{"blob":"9e55ea8c9823c34b72d58173fc1273593d246733","intervals":[[1,1048]],"path":"apps/crq-python/crq_repair.py"},{"blob":"74a2394df9a75c96217fb3d9c956515da6727530","intervals":[[1,446]],"path":"apps/crq-python/repair_snapshot_vectors.py"},{"blob":"cbc5c62ae6c4bd5ab414a23596c9842785a0c5f7","intervals":[[1,1305]],"path":"apps/crq-python/repair_tick.py"},{"blob":"a2ba772ec9193e9fd96fb356044c265e41af9ec3","intervals":[[1,325]],"path":"apps/crq-python/test_deploy_controller_cli.py"}],"job_id":"b59d2eadfa473b51e69a70ad27a6090f2240f5ed27b9ecb9da5847782c22225e:0","outcome":"completed","paths":[{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"9e55ea8c9823c34b72d58173fc1273593d246733","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"apps/crq-python/crq_repair.py","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"74a2394df9a75c96217fb3d9c956515da6727530","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"apps/crq-python/repair_snapshot_vectors.py","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"cbc5c62ae6c4bd5ab414a23596c9842785a0c5f7","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"apps/crq-python/repair_tick.py","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"a2ba772ec9193e9fd96fb356044c265e41af9ec3","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"apps/crq-python/test_deploy_controller_cli.py","reason":"bounded verified input"}],"policy_digest":"eacd1bcf42a0e72eca72fcf9c1e9c8f97e7c515cd67a8fa7965c966924647693","repo":"camerontaylor/cq-toolkit","requested_sco